lessons.body:
Signed Standard Uploads for Small
Files
TaskFlow - Full Stack Developer 2026

When to use it
Supabase recommends standard uploads for small files and TUS resumable uploads when files exceed
roughly 6MB, network reliability matters, or progress events are required.

API creates an intent
async createIntent(taskId: string, user: AuthenticatedUser, input: CreateAttachmentIntent) {
const task = await this.tasks.findScopedById(taskId, user.id)
if (!task) throw new TaskNotFoundException(taskId)

const attachmentId = randomUUID()
const objectPath = buildAttachmentObjectPath({
workspaceId: task.workspaceId,
taskId,
attachmentId,
mimeType: input.mimeType,
})

const row = await this.attachments.createPending({
id: attachmentId,
taskId,
uploadedById: user.id,
bucket: ATTACHMENT_BUCKET,
objectPath,
...input,
})

try {
const signed = await this.storage.createSignedUploadUrl(objectPath)
return { attachment: row, upload: signed }
} catch (error) {
await this.attachments.deletePending(attachmentId)
throw error
}
}

Browser transfers bytes
const { error } = await supabase.storage
.from(intent.attachment.bucket)
.uploadToSignedUrl(
intent.attachment.objectPath,
intent.upload.token,
file,
{ contentType: file.type },
)

if (error) throw error

await completeAttachment(intent.attachment.id)

No upsert by default
Each attachment gets a new UUID path, so overwriting is unnecessary. Supabase also
recommends new paths instead of overwrites to avoid stale CDN propagation behavior.

