Frontend UX, TanStack Query and
Form Integration
TaskFlow - Full Stack Developer 2026

UI responsibilities
• Validate obvious type/size issues before requesting an intent.

• Show selected filename and human-readable size.

• Show transfer progress for TUS uploads.

• Distinguish uploading from finalizing.

• Allow retry without creating uncontrolled duplicate records.

• Announce errors and progress accessibly.

Mutation lifecycle
const uploadAttachment = useMutation({
mutationFn: async (file: File) => {
const intent = await createAttachmentIntent(taskId, file)
await uploadFile(intent, file, setProgress)
return completeAttachment(intent.attachment.id)
},

onSuccess: async () => {
await queryClient.invalidateQueries({
queryKey: attachmentKeys.list(taskId),
})
},
})

State ownership
• Selected File and progress: local component/mutation UI state.

• Attachment list: TanStack Query server state.

• Upload policy: shared display hints may exist client-side, but NestJS and bucket restrictions remain
authoritative.

• Original filename field: display metadata, not a storage key.

Accessibility
Use a real file input with a programmatic label, provide text progress in addition to a visual bar, and
announce success/failure through a polite status region. Do not communicate upload state only by
color.

